# Repo-root environment — copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. This file is the committed template.
#
# ─── Turbo remote cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository reads its turbo credentials from `.env` and NOWHERE else.
# They are deliberately NOT taken from your shell environment: a single
# `export TURBO_TEAM=...` in a shell profile applies to every repo on the
# machine, which is how a personal project ends up writing to an unrelated
# team's cache. Keeping the values in this file scopes them to this repo.
#
# To fill these in, run once in your terminal:
#
#   turbo login && turbo link
#
# `turbo link` writes `.turbo/config.json` (gitignored) with this repo's team
# ID. That file is what the orchestrator's guard checks TURBO_TEAM against, so
# the two must agree or the remote cache is disabled.
#
# Note: `turbo login` does NOT export anything into your shell — it only writes
# `~/.turbo/config.json`. Copy the values here by hand.
#
# Read `.turbo/config.json` for the team ID, and `~/.turbo/config.json` for the
# token.
TURBO_TOKEN=
TURBO_TEAM=

# ─── Error reporting (Bugsink) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are OPTIONAL and both are EMPTY here on purpose. `@gate/logger` forwards
# every `logger.error()` call to a reporter; with no DSN the Sentry SDK is never
# even loaded, no reporter is installed, and the apps behave exactly as they do
# today. That is what keeps local runs, CI and the sandbox indifferent to this
# wiring — the deployed values live in Vercel's project settings, not here.
#
# Two variables because the browser and the server are separate realms and the
# reporter slot cannot cross between them. A Sentry-style DSN is submit-only, so
# the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` one is safe in a public client bundle; abuse control is
# Bugsink's per-project rate limiting.
#
# The public one is inlined into the client bundle at build time, so it is named
# in `turbo.json`'s `build.env` — same reason `VERCEL_ENV` is. The server one is
# read at request time and deliberately is NOT, so changing it does not
# invalidate a build.
BUGSINK_DSN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_BUGSINK_DSN=
